Filter applied to the source's 1,000,000 lines, in this order
  1. Keep entries of 12 or more characters (Unicode characters, not bytes).
     Shorter passwords are already refused by the minimum length.
  2. Drop email-shaped entries: those matching ^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$
     (one "@" with text before it, and a dotted domain after it).
  3. Drop exact duplicates, keeping the first (highest-ranked) occurrence.
  Rank order is preserved. Entries are written as they appear in the source
  (no trimming, no case change); the application compares case-insensitively.

Result
  31,102 lines, 29,940 distinct once lowercased.

